  "question": {
    "text": "A current through a wire depends on time as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>,&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Find the charge crossed through a section of the wire in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo></math>"
